# DTF tier manifest: scan-on-proxy-cocoapods-swift  (artifact-keeper 1.12.0:
# #4109 CocoaPods, #4110 Swift, epic #4097)
# Profile-set: filesystem + the mock-scan-formats upstream (a CocoaPods pod
# source and a Swift registry whose archives carry known contents).
# LOCAL-ONLY: the verdicts come from the backend image's bundled Grype and its
# pre-seeded vulnerability DB (no scanner sidecar, no OSV, no internet).
#
# WHAT IT GUARDS: before 1.12.0 a CocoaPods or Swift Remote (or a Virtual over
# one) with scan_on_proxy=true streamed every proxied archive unscanned (200,
# no X-AK-Scan) and /api/v1/formats reported both as `accepted`. 1.12.0 routes
# pod archives and Swift source archives through the shared inline scan gate,
# graded on their contents (the bundled scanner has no advisory data for
# either ecosystem, so the vulnerable fixtures vendor a Gemfile.lock):
# vulnerable -> 403 scan_blocked, clean -> 200 X-AK-Scan: clean with the
# verdict reused, an archive that does not back the request -> 423 under
# fail_closed with no verdict row.
#
# Red: ak-backend:1.11.5. Green: an image carrying artifact-keeper#4109-#4110.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-scan-formats"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
